Description:
Bluechiip, a Cryonix Group Brand, is a leader in the development of advanced sample management solutions, understands that every biological sample is critical, so our objective is to manage each one with optimal quality in the most efficient way. Bluechiip provides a range of products and services across clinical research, drug development and advanced cell therapies to support the world’s leading laboratories across pharmaceutical, biotech and academic institutes globally.

Bluechiip’s Advanced Sample Management Solution and patented technology stack operates across all, extreme (from –196°C to +150°C) temperatures, enabling unmatched accuracy, traceability, and real-time data capture at the individual sample level. Its integrated system of enabled cryogenic vials, smart readers, and cloud-based software delivers a fully digitized sample management workflow - eliminating manual data entry, improving regulatory compliance, and dramatically increasing productivity.

Key advantages of Bluechiip product offerings include:
# True cold-chain tracking from storage to bench, with live sample temperature and location data;
# Plug-and-play compatibility with existing workflows and digital tools (e.g. ELN, LIMS);
# Rapid deployment without the need for custom software or IT infrastructure;
# Scalable and cost-efficient alternative to fully automated freezer systems; and
# Enhanced traceability and security for critical assets in biobanking, cell therapy, IVF, clinical trials, and pharma R&D.

Please note that this page now reflects the assets and brand of Bluechiip under the ownership by Cryonix Group. Previous company roles listed here may not reflect current affiliations. For more information, refer to the Cryonix Group page.

Aliquot Solutions has extensive experience with Contract Research Labs. With our deep scientific understanding, strong networks and commercial acumen, we can help source the right lab for your testing, or help your lab to expand.

Catherine Osborne, the founder of Aliquot Solutions, is a PhD-trained biologist with many years of industry experience providing excellent service to researchers and the clinical ecosystem.

Catherine loves connecting clients with the best scientific solutions. She takes prides in providing the smoothest client experience when selecting the best labs, or helping scientists turn their technical services into great businesses.

Commercial services we can provide to Contract Labs include market research, business case analysis, vendor management, business development and sourcing investment. Our technical understanding of the specialty testing options available, especially for genomics and immunology, can speed up your lab vendor management.

Aliquot Solutions is proudly based in Australia, a booming destination for clinical trials, with its:
- efficient regulatory systems, such as 30 day approval process for Phase I and no need for IND;
- advanced healthcare infrastructure and interconnected service providers;
- diverse population and educated workforce;
- and the R&D Tax Incentive, with 43.5% cash back on eligible activities, such as clinical trial costs.

VAXMED is an Australian, privately-owned biotechnology company developing novel vaccines for infectious diseases, based in Melbourne and Adelaide.
We use complex computer algorithms to design and develop highly effective vaccines and a state-of-the-art production process. Our vaccines are fully synthetic and designed to provide long lasting immunity in a single shot vaccination and at the same time, broad-spectrum cover against multiple virus strains or infectious diseases.
Our proprietary manufacturing technology is designed to produce 100s of millions of doses from each batch run in a matter of weeks.
Unlike most other vaccines, VAXMED vaccines do not require consistent cold storage and temperature control from manufacture through to point of use. They can be stored at room temperature when freeze dried, many years.
VAXMED’s vaccines and novel technology has been independently evaluated by leading global vaccine experts, both in industry and academia as one of the most promising in the field.
The VAXMED product pipeline includes
   A universal influenza vaccine which will cover all seasonal strains, future pandemic strains without the need to reformulate the vaccine each season;
   Respiratory Syncytial Virus (RSV) a major cause of lower respiratory tract infections in children and the elderly  worldwide; 
   Dual Staphylococcus and Pseudomonas (ventilator-associated pneumonia, chronic pulmonary infection in cystic fibrosis patients, and burn and soft tissue infections);
   Universal Coronavirus, a vaccine protective against most Coronaviruses including COVID-19, the previous SARS virus, Middle Eastern Respiratory Syndrome (MERS), and other human Coronaviruses that cause common colds and potentially future outbreaks;
   African Swine Fever (AFS) which AFS is a major problem in Asia, Europe and Africa affecting the pig industry.

Clinical Research Consulting
- Experience in clinical trial phases I-IV, including interventional non-interventional, observational and registries;
- Provide clinical operational support with any or all aspects of the clinical study life cycle;
- Support includes trial and study project management, contract research organisation (CRO) management, vendor management (data management, biostatistics, medical writing, laboratory, IMP).
